{
  "name": "Turn call and chat transcripts into structured sales records with Claude, Google Sheets and Gmail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "259c2a57-ff2e-443a-bb8c-1771cc162891",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -384,
        -16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 816,
        "content": "## Turn call and chat transcripts into structured sales records with Claude, Google Sheets and Gmail\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow accepts pasted conversations or API-submitted call/chat transcripts, normalizes the input, and sends it to Claude for structured sales-record extraction. It parses Claude’s response into usable views, logs the structured conversation record to Google Sheets, optionally alerts the team by Gmail when the record is urgent, and returns either JSON for API calls or a results page for form submissions.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Anthropic/Claude credentials and choose the desired Claude model for the AI extraction node.\n- Set up the Google Sheets credential and map the destination spreadsheet/table used by the conversation records log.\n- Configure Gmail credentials and verify the alert recipient field or default team email address.\n- Review the form trigger and webhook URL so the expected transcript fields are supplied consistently to the Normalize Input step.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Claude prompt and parsing code to change which sales fields are extracted, update the urgency condition to match your escalation rules, and modify the Google Sheets columns or Gmail alert copy for your team’s process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "14424ce9-e442-49ea-a430-a4a5d7b4a952",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        176,
        -16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 624,
        "content": "## Conversation intake\n\nProvides two entry points for transcripts: a manual form paste and an API webhook. The nearby normalization code standardizes both sources into a common format for downstream processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2a59311e-4a42-4b2f-8c4e-134aa938b5fd",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        704,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 624,
        "content": "## AI extraction\n\nSends the normalized conversation to Claude and parses the model output into structured sales-record data and presentation-friendly views."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7fadd5cc-586b-4819-9362-d37e27b3ef7f",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1232,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Prepare and log record\n\nAdds the alert-recipient value and writes the completed structured conversation record to Google Sheets for tracking and reporting."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3326d18f-e9f4-4225-bc0e-19bed985c794",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1760,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 464,
        "content": "## Urgency alerting\n\nChecks whether the parsed conversation is urgent and, when needed, sends an email alert to the team before continuing the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c506dcb8-d7c4-4c13-be00-139d892ea5ca",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2272,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 576,
        "content": "## Return final output\n\nDetermines whether the original submission came from the API or the form, then returns structured JSON to webhook callers or displays a results page to form users."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7bb5a054-467d-4967-a1c0-a72552399d9d",
      "name": "When Form is Submitted",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "position": [
        220,
        160
      ],
      "webhookId": "061974e6-b1d9-4b29-a8ce-9d82efd94b26",
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "buttonLabel": "Analyze"
        },
        "formTitle": "Conversation Analyzer",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldName": "transcript",
              "fieldType": "textarea",
              "fieldLabel": "Transcript",
              "placeholder": "Paste the raw conversation here",
              "requiredField": true
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "channel",
